# Curriculum and Cost: Notes on the Utilization of Teaching Resources.

**Authors:** Zemsky, Robert

## Abstract
The article reports preliminary observations on data from six colleges on application of a regression model to help explain observed differences in instructional efficiencies of specific curricula. A major finding was that the most efficient distribution of students is in the humanities and social sciences. Tentative explanations for this finding are offered. (DB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ418500

